        "label": "Script: every surface",
        "color": "amber",
        "body": "One Script per socket family it can read, one per result type and rank it can return. A Script is a JavaScript function: its parameters are the inputs, its return value is folded onto the declared result type. Number, text, boolean and date values arrive as plain JS values (a date is its serial), lists as arrays, tables as arrays of rows, complex numbers as {re, im}. Frames, cubes, lambdas, charts and documents stay out: those are the verb engine's and the figures' business.",
